WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.983
This map reached the public in three

2
00:00:02.063 --> 00:00:04.792
distinct forms. Levent Alpöge posted the explicit

3
00:00:04.872 --> 00:00:07.773
polynomial formula, crediting Akhil for the question

4
00:00:07.853 --> 00:00:09.780
and Fable for the work. Later, Andy

5
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.990
Jiang, at davikrehalt, posted the projective marked-root

6
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.627
description and explicitly presented it as GPT

7
00:00:15.707 --> 00:00:18.206
output. Aaron Lou then gave a resultant-based

8
00:00:18.286 --> 00:00:21.130
derivation and global affine chart. This repository

9
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:24.742
compiles, explains, visualizes, and checks those contributions.

10
00:00:25.266 --> 00:00:27.510
The Jacobian condition is local: at every

11
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:30.400
finite point, the derivative is invertible. Imagine

12
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.950
a tiny neighborhood being moved without being

13
00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.614
pinched flat. The surprise is global. Different

14
00:00:35.694 --> 00:00:37.938
distant points can still acquire the same

15
00:00:38.018 --> 00:00:40.941
image if inverse branches disappear through infinity.

16
00:00:41.021 --> 00:00:42.868
That is the mechanism we will see.

17
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.837
Alpöge's presentation begins with three explicit polynomials

18
00:00:46.917 --> 00:00:48.595
in x, y, and z. Exact symbolic

19
00:00:48.675 --> 00:00:51.702
expansion gives determinant minus two everywhere. The

20
00:00:51.782 --> 00:00:54.222
formula is the fastest certificate that the

21
00:00:54.302 --> 00:00:56.567
map is locally invertible, but by itself

22
00:00:56.647 --> 00:00:58.971
it gives little clue why these particular

23
00:00:59.051 --> 00:01:00.084
terms fit together.

24
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.079
Now substitute these three source points. They

25
00:01:03.159 --> 00:01:05.026
are distinct, yet every one maps to

26
00:01:05.106 --> 00:01:07.585
negative one quarter, zero, zero. This already

27
00:01:07.665 --> 00:01:10.979
proves noninjectivity. The remaining descriptions explain the

28
00:01:11.059 --> 00:01:13.372
hidden object that each point is recording.

29
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.864
A cubic has three projective roots when multiplicity

30
00:01:16.944 --> 00:01:19.615
is counted. Temporarily mark one root and leave

31
00:01:19.695 --> 00:01:22.016
the other two unordered. For a cubic with

32
00:01:22.096 --> 00:01:25.177
three distinct roots, there are exactly three possible

33
00:01:25.257 --> 00:01:27.636
markings. If we now forget the mark, those

34
00:01:27.716 --> 00:01:30.680
three choices become one cubic. Generic degree three

35
00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.080
is therefore built into the construction.

36
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.352
Jiang's post packages this as a projective map.

37
00:01:36.432 --> 00:01:38.401
A point p and an unordered pair q,

38
00:01:38.481 --> 00:01:40.631
r are sent to the unordered triple p,

39
00:01:40.711 --> 00:01:43.524
q, r. In symbols, projective one-space times its

40
00:01:43.604 --> 00:01:46.537
second symmetric power maps to its third symmetric

41
00:01:46.617 --> 00:01:49.490
power. This is simply the operation: forget which

42
00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:50.876
root was distinguished.

43
00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.520
The forgetful map ramifies only when the

44
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.501
marked root collides with one of the

45
00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:58.362
two residual roots. Delete exactly that ramification

46
00:01:58.442 --> 00:02:00.838
divisor. The unmarked roots may still collide

47
00:02:00.918 --> 00:02:03.533
with each other. After deletion, the differential

48
00:02:03.613 --> 00:02:06.009
is invertible everywhere that remains, so the

49
00:02:06.089 --> 00:02:07.330
restricted map is étale.

50
00:02:07.866 --> 00:02:10.008
Next choose a hyperplane tangent, but

51
00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:12.230
not osculating, to the small diagonal

52
00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.272
of triple roots. Its complement in

53
00:02:14.352 --> 00:02:17.695
projective three-space is affine three-space. Remarkably,

54
00:02:17.775 --> 00:02:20.278
the corresponding source complement is also

55
00:02:20.358 --> 00:02:23.220
affine three-space. Choosing coordinates on these

56
00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.623
two spaces turns the geometric forgetful

57
00:02:25.703 --> 00:02:27.604
map into Alpöge's polynomial map.

58
00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:31.435
Lou's description replaces a marked root by a factorization

59
00:02:31.515 --> 00:02:33.958
of the binary cubic: a linear factor ell for

60
00:02:34.038 --> 00:02:36.653
the marked root, times a quadratic factor q for

61
00:02:36.733 --> 00:02:39.634
the other two. But the factorization has a redundant

62
00:02:39.714 --> 00:02:41.813
scale. Multiplying ell by s and q by s

63
00:02:41.893 --> 00:02:43.819
inverse leaves the cubic unchanged.

64
00:02:44.333 --> 00:02:47.876
The linear-quadratic resultant detects whether the marked root

65
00:02:47.956 --> 00:02:50.272
is simple. It is nonzero exactly when ell

66
00:02:50.352 --> 00:02:52.376
and q have no common root. Under the

67
00:02:52.456 --> 00:02:55.415
redundant scaling, the resultant is multiplied by s.

68
00:02:55.495 --> 00:02:58.571
Requiring resultant one therefore chooses one and only

69
00:02:58.651 --> 00:03:02.019
one representative on every simple-root scaling orbit. This

70
00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:03.363
is the resultant gauge.

71
00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.897
These are not competing maps. They are

72
00:03:05.977 --> 00:03:08.412
three coordinate systems for one arrow. Alpöge

73
00:03:08.492 --> 00:03:11.201
gives the direct formula and collision certificate.

74
00:03:11.281 --> 00:03:13.716
Jiang and GPT expose the marked-root geometry.

75
00:03:13.796 --> 00:03:16.122
Lou supplies the normalized factor space and

76
00:03:16.202 --> 00:03:18.473
global affine chart. Lou's coordinate map G

77
00:03:18.553 --> 00:03:20.496
equals an output reversal after F and

78
00:03:20.576 --> 00:03:22.300
a sign change in the source. That

79
00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:25.089
is left-right equivalence, not dynamical conjugacy.

80
00:03:25.633 --> 00:03:29.103
Complex three-space has six real dimensions, so here

81
00:03:29.183 --> 00:03:32.517
we visualize only its real slice. Three elementary

82
00:03:32.597 --> 00:03:36.067
source curves are mapped exactly: the x-axis becomes

83
00:03:36.147 --> 00:03:39.139
a target line, the y-axis becomes a parabola,

84
00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:42.348
and the z-axis becomes another target line. The

85
00:03:42.428 --> 00:03:45.557
same formulas drive both this animation and the

86
00:03:45.637 --> 00:03:46.718
browser artifact.

87
00:03:47.266 --> 00:03:50.213
A more revealing target curve represents cubics with

88
00:03:50.293 --> 00:03:52.308
roots zero, s, and one minus s. Each

89
00:03:52.388 --> 00:03:55.451
possible marked root defines a different source curve,

90
00:03:55.531 --> 00:03:57.547
but all three map to the same target

91
00:03:57.627 --> 00:04:00.166
curve. As s approaches zero, two marked roots

92
00:04:00.246 --> 00:04:03.367
collide. Their two source branches run toward infinity,

93
00:04:03.447 --> 00:04:06.277
while the branch marking the remaining simple root

94
00:04:06.357 --> 00:04:09.013
stays finite. No finite critical point appears.

95
00:04:09.633 --> 00:04:11.360
The proof now has a short spine.

96
00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.521
Both chosen complements are affine three-space. Removing

97
00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:17.627
marked-root ramification makes the forgetful map étale.

98
00:04:17.707 --> 00:04:19.829
A general cubic has three simple roots,

99
00:04:19.909 --> 00:04:21.805
so the map has generic degree three

100
00:04:21.885 --> 00:04:24.910
and cannot be injective. Constant Jacobian, three-point

101
00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.168
fibers, and escape at infinity are three

102
00:04:27.248 --> 00:04:29.596
views of the same geometry. Adding identity

103
00:04:29.676 --> 00:04:32.871
coordinates extends the construction to higher dimensions,

104
00:04:32.951 --> 00:04:35.524
while dimension two remains a separate problem.
